# The encoder is committed; the payload it reads and the container it writes are
# not. DOOM1.WAD is copyrighted shareware data (and 4,196,020 B, larger than the
# whole flash), and every .whd here is a repacked copy of it. Point the tool at a
# WAD outside the repository and write containers outside the repository too;
# this file is the guard for the day someone forgets.
*.WAD
*.wad
*.whd
*.WHD

# Python leaves bytecode behind when a probe imports whd_encode as a module.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
